  ],
  "fact_notes": [
    "オリジナル論説・架空事例。実在の調査結果・歴史資料・機器の実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A student finds a photograph in a box of family records.",
          "ja": "生徒が家族の記録の箱で写真を見つける。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It shows several people standing outside a building that no longer exists.",
          "ja": "今は存在しない建物の外に数人が立っている様子を示す。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A date is written on the back in blue ink.",
          "ja": "裏には青いインクで日付が書かれている。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The student assumes that this is the date on which the photograph was taken.",
          "ja": "生徒は撮影日だと思う。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "During a conversation with a relative, she learns that the photograph was given to the family many years after the building was removed.",
          "ja": "親族との会話で建物が撤去されて何年も後に写真が家族へ渡されたと知る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The relative remembers receiving the photograph at a gathering, but cannot remember who wrote the date.",
          "ja": "親族は集まりで写真を受け取ったことを覚えているが誰が日付を書いたか覚えていない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The student begins to wonder whether the date refers to the original event or to something that happened later.",
          "ja": "日付は当初の出来事を指すのか後の出来事を指すのか疑問に思い始める。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The photograph itself does not provide enough information to settle this question.",
          "ja": "写真自体は問いを解決する十分な情報を提供しない。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "She decides to compare the photograph with other available records.",
          "ja": "写真を他の利用可能な記録と比較することを決める。"
        },
        {
          "en": "An old drawing shows the same building with a different entrance.",
          "ja": "古い絵は異なる入口を持つ同じ建物を示す。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A written account describes changes made to the building at a particular time.",
          "ja": "記述資料は特定の時期に行われた建物の変更を説明する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "These materials may help identify a possible period, although neither immediately establishes an exact date.",
          "ja": "資料は可能な時期の特定に役立つかもしれないがどちらもすぐ正確な日付を確定しない。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The student prepares a school report separating observations from interpretations.",
          "ja": "観察と解釈を区別する学校レポートを作る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She explains what can be seen in the photograph and what the relative remembers.",
          "ja": "写真で見えることと親族が覚えていることを説明する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She also describes the evidence that would be needed to confirm her preferred explanation.",
          "ja": "好ましい説明を確認するために必要な証拠も記述する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Her teacher encourages her to keep the uncertain date visible rather than silently replacing it with a guess.",
          "ja": "教師は推測に黙って置き換えず不確実な日付を明示するよう促す。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A historical object may contain information added at several different times.",
          "ja": "歴史的な物には複数の異なる時期に追加された情報が含まれることがある。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Its meaning cannot always be understood by treating every detail as part of one original event.",
          "ja": "全細部を一つの当初出来事の一部と扱っても意味は常に理解できない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Learning about the history of a record can be just as important as learning about the event it describes.",
          "ja": "記録の来歴は記述された出来事を学ぶことと同じほど重要になり得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The date on the photograph becomes the beginning of an investigation rather than its conclusion.",
          "ja": "写真の日付は調査の結論でなく始まりになる。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
